.TH LINKDUPES 1 "October 2026" "add-determinism 0.7.3" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
linkdupes \- replace identical files with hard links
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B linkdupes
.RI [ options ] " path ..."
.SH DESCRIPTION
Compare file content and metadata recursively and hardlink matching files.
Ownership, permissions, timestamps and SELinux contexts are checked by default.
Symbolic links are not followed.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --brp
Use RPM build root checks and treat processing errors as fatal.
.TP
.BR -n , " --dry-run"
Report the links that would be created without modifying files.
.TP
.B --ignore-mtime
Allow files with different modification times to be linked.
.TP
.B --ignore-mode
Allow files with different access modes to be linked.
.TP
.B --ignore-owner
Allow files with different owners or groups to be linked.
.TP
.B --ignore-selinux-context
Disable SELinux context comparisons.
.TP
.B --print-selinux-contexts
Print SELinux contexts.
.TP
.BR -v , " --verbose"
Increase diagnostic output. May be repeated.
.TP
.BR -V , " --version"
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR -h , " --help"
Print command help and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
RPM_BUILD_ROOT identifies the build root when --brp is used.
SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH clamps timestamps for comparison when set.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR add-det (1)
